The projects collection is defined in src/content.config.ts and is empty on
purpose: the placeholder entry was deleted in phase 3 and real work lands in
phase 6. Git does not track empty directories, so this file keeps the loader's
base directory present.

The build still warns that nothing matches "**/*.md". That warning is correct
— the collection is empty — and it goes away when the first real project is
added. The loader only reads .md, so this file is never content.
